<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad II of Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1235">1235</a>–<a href="/years/1302">1302</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad II al-Faqih</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad II was the second Nasrid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, reigning from 1273 to 1302. He organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>'s administration and defended it by playing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, Aragon and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> against one another. He welcomed North African volunteer troops into Granada's service and secured the kingdom against Castilian pressure.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Muhammad II</b> and his successors played Castile, Aragon and the Marinids against one another, at times losing or recovering ports such as Tarifa, Algeciras and Gibraltar.</blockquote><a href="/empire/emirate-of-granada">Emirate of Granada · Military</a></li></ul></section>
